          "english_quote": "and besides not suffering, you will find him able to heal others as well.",
          "issue": "The supplied reading has nominative δυνάμενος, whereas the English predicates the ability of the person represented by accusative αὐτὸν. The ensuing example of Moses healing others supports this contextual interpretation of the irregular construction, so the rendering need not be blocked. Nevertheless, the case mismatch and the material alternative attachment to the addressed person are not disclosed anywhere in the draft notes.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a note quoting the supplied construction exactly. Explain that the main rendering understands the healing ability as belonging to the sinless person despite the printed nominative, with the following Moses example supporting that choice. Preserve the alternative nominative attachment to the addressee: approximately, “you, being able to heal others as well, may find him.” Do not silently replace δυνάμενος with δυνάμενον or characterize the verified print as an OCR error. The revised text and notes require fresh review.",
