          "english_quote": "For we have seen your defeat in action and have heard your promised argument.",
          "issue": "“Have heard your promised argument” naturally suggests that the substantive argument Simon promised has already been heard. That does not clearly represent the contrast between defeat demonstrated in action and promise-making speech merely heard. The draft's note expressly says the argument has not already been delivered, but the main wording fails to communicate that distinction. The following prediction that Simon will not return further supports rendering the heard λόγος as words of promise.",
